  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Allow the ability of who created the instance of the world to set a description/theme of what is going on in that world. And or their own status message in game. Let everyone know if that world just has people hanging out, testing avatars, having a dance party, drawing memes, what ever it may be. I believe it would make more sense to put that message on the instance of the world it's self. The creator of the instance might leave but what ever people are doing in there usually won't change from my experience. This surely could increase the amount of worlds made public and the amount of people joining public worlds. If I knew for example if I saw  people were having a mute dance party in a public presentation room I would join that.",
